# Profile notes: primary claims use the did:demos:agent ClaimReference profile
# (src/catalog/claimRef.ts), which the pinned revision does not yet define. It comes from
# DACS-Standard #296, merged into `next` at 725fa78bd124a7adb65df27adee376d5d44a4bd7; its fixture
# is vendored below. Its keys are Ed25519, so artifacts signed with ecdsa-secp256k1 or
# sr1-aggregate cannot be verified under this profile and are not published or counted.
# Recorded deviations (vectors: test/standard-vectors.test.ts; local guards: test/evidence-graph-rules.test.ts,
# test/indexer-binding-rules.test.ts, test/legacy-deal-rules.test.ts and test/native-payment.test.ts):
#   §8.5.2 checks 5-6 need the CommitmentRecord's anchored committedAt, which a bundle does not
#     reference: a session whose listing sets deadlineSecAfterCommit or validity.notAfter is
#     indeterminate and never counted.
#   CD-1: a non-canonical amount (e.g. "95.00") is rejected rather than canonicalised (fail-closed).
#   agreement-listing-v0.1 `fractional-pct-out` expects reject; the §8.5.2 text (round to the CD-1
#     digits of bandCenter) accepts it, and the Directory follows the text.
#   SB-1: pinned evm/x402 refs omit logIndex; Solana refs omit instructionIndex. These refs are
#     error and never counted. AP2, htlc-* and liquidity-tank refs have no SB-1 key format and are
#     likewise uncounted (HTLC-5 session binding is not an SB-1 key). Every legacy SDK evm-erc20
#     or x402 deal is uncounted because its TxRef lacks the event index; only legacy pay-dem keys.
#   Authoritative bundle absence: the Demos mapping declares no absence-evidence policy. Both
#     absence sets below run; their policy-qualified one-sided pass/include cases deliberately
#     remain indeterminate/excluded. No Directory endpoint authenticates those projected proofs.
#   Vet admission resolves historical IdentityBundle bytes and checks the presentation/hash. This
#     profile can read a signed BundleParty extension `identityBundle` (inline) or
#     `identityBundleRef` (storage-program locator and IdentityBundle hash), or use
#     EvidenceGraphDeps.resolveIdentityBundle. Publication self-bindings cannot supply session identity.
#     IdentityBundle hashes omit presentation per DACS-1. Session Vet additionally requires a trusted
#     resolveSessionChallenge adapter authenticating verifier issuance, job/party/nonce, challenge
#     lifetime, authenticated consumedAt and the hash of the first consuming presentation attempt
#     (CORE SN-1..4). IdentityBundle.presentedAt is schema-checked but informational.
#     No production historical-challenge resolver is installed: those sessions remain indeterminate.
#     Listing publication continues to accept a nonce-free signed self-binding.
#   Required credential matching uses the signed composite generatedAt (unix ms) as the historical
#     Vet instant, bounded by finalisedAt; it does not expire old sessions against the wall clock.
#     validUntil governs; without it, DACS_RECIPE_POLICIES must supply defaultMaxAgeSec for the exact
#     scheme/recipeVersion. Every required result, including one with validUntil, also needs an
#     live exact-version recipe policy, an allowed method and a trusted authenticated signer.
#     RAV-2: the catalog does not disclose per-result availability yet. Non-live vet results
#     remain indeterminate; non-live recipes cannot elevate identity tiers either. This applies
#     to every included VerifyResult, optional ones too: each needs a valid live recipe policy.
#     Wrapper expiry and listing maxAge only narrow that authority window.
#     No scheme-specific requirement-parameter interpreter is configured: non-empty parameters
#     are unmatched, as DACS-1 requires for unrecognised parameters, rather than inferred from data.
#   DV-1..3: storage delivery resolves object cleartext and node ACL metadata. The DV-1 hash covers
#     the complete NFC/JCS payload, including any signature/signatures fields (the pinned SDK's
#     contentHash strips them; the Standard's lifecycle walkthrough does not). Unreadable payloads,
#     encrypt-to-buyer payloads (no buyer decryption capability), and external pointer payloads
#     (no external cleartext resolver) remain indeterminate and never count as completion/volume.
#   Rail admission uses explicitly provisioned DACS_RAIL_SNAPSHOTS (PA-1 operator trust).
#     Snapshots pin registryVersion and railVersion, handler, asset, network, parameters and availability.
#     Operators must authenticate the registry index/definitions before provisioning; no snapshot is
#     bundled or inferred from a listing or RPC. Unknown versions remain indeterminate. Only a live
#     demos-native:DEM definition with native-dem/DEM/9 and network demos can use the native adapter.
#   Native pay-dem: success additionally requires blockNumber and getTxByHash/getBlockByNumber
#     reads establishing confirmed inclusion, native-send endpoints and the exact DEM price in OS.
#     Stored RPC amounts are numeric/string OS; the original send payload must carry canonical string OS.
#     Numeric legacy DEM payloads need historical fork semantics and remain indeterminate. Unavailable reads never count. The node source calls terminal inclusion "confirmed".
#   Attested-payload and entitlement success remain indeterminate until authoritative attestation
#     and grant adapters can establish their agreement-bound proofs; signatures alone do not count.
#   All non-native current rails and paid SDK legacy sessions remain indeterminate without authoritative
#     adapters; they never contribute completion or volume. AP2 and x402 success is indeterminate: this profile has no authenticated provider-receipt
#     resolver. A signed receipt pointer/hash alone cannot establish provider or HTTP settlement.
#   Current publisher rail IDs are demos-native:DEM and x402:default. Historical signed phase-name
#     aliases remain readable for evidence, but public discovery excludes those current offers;
#     their publisher must issue a new signed version. Legacy SDK rail names retain that profile.
#   Anonymous restricted-program reads on node ac8f45f are denied: buyer-only is indeterminate
#     on that deployment. ACL-success tests model a hypothetical readable metadata contract.
#   Revocation candidates: discovered markers returning NOT_FOUND, PERMISSION_DENIED or a transport
#     failure stay pending/indeterminate. Persistent 1–60 second exponential backoff bounds retries.
#     Only successfully read invalid content can reject a candidate; verified revocation is retained.
#   Per-claim PresentationSignature.signature retains the SDK auto-detected legacy encoding;
#     strict SIG-6 value-envelope decoding is enforced separately.
# Skipped vector sets at this pin:
#   private-deliverables-v0.1: projected cci/40-byte buyer addresses and encryption/entitlement
#     gates do not map directly to this agent profile; signed local graph cases pin DV-1..3.
#   verifyresult-acceptance-v0.1: recipe-registry steward signatures and cci claims are outside
#     the deployment-policy recipe adapter; local vet/recipe tests pin the supported profile.
#   fab-bundle-extended-pointer-v0.3: no external extended-pointer resolver.
#   settlement-finalization-propagation-v0.3 and receipt-rederivation-v0.3: handler-side
